<article about="/en/ranking-criteria-for-incoming-student-mobility" typeof="schema:WebPage" class="node node--type-page node--view-mode-full" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/WebPage">
    <meta itemprop="name" content="Ranking criteria for incoming student mobility">

            <div class="field-introduction--wrapper">
            
            <div class="field field--name-field-introduction field--type-string-long field--label-hidden field__item" itemprop="description">The International Committee at Nord approved the following criteria for ranking of incoming exchange students (ref. meeting 13/09/2023)</div>
      
        </div>
        
    <div class="node__content">
        <div class="main-content">

            
            <div property="schema:text" class="field--text-long field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item">




<main class="wp-block-drupal-section">
<p>Ranking criteria for incoming student mobility:</p>



<ol><li>Students coming from SEA-EU partner institutions are prioritized in accordance with<br>the number of exchange places specified in each individual agreement.</li><li>Priority for mobility reciprocity: Partner institutions accepting students from Nord will be prioritized for the remaining exchange places so that reciprocity is ensured.</li><li>Raffle draw, on the individual international student and not partner institution. Only<br>candidates who are not prioritized through point 1 and point 2, are valid for a raffle<br>draw.</li></ol>
</main>
</div>
      
            
